60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option A looks great! Local items mean low shipping costs, and the interviews are a dynamic touch that doesn't cost a fortune!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Option A is the only sustainable choice. It doesn't require the conservation lab to clear its backlog, and the craftspeople can help with the work.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shion,,"Option A and D both have the human element I'm looking for. However, D's ""working bench"" is a brilliant way to keep people coming back to see progress.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option B is out of the question; the overhead rigging and powered works are a disaster waiting to happen. Option D is too heavy with reconstructions. Option A is the safest.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Option A seems very peaceful and reliable. Since the items are local, we won't have to worry about shipping delays or paperwork mishaps.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shion, wouldn't the demonstration sessions in Option A be just as exciting as the conservation bench in Option D?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shion, Option D's ""working bench"" is a fantasy. The lab is already overwhelmed; we cannot turn it into a public performance space. It would be a nightmare for the staff.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Victoria, your fear of work is stifling. But I admit, if the staff is truly that broken, the ""working bench"" might just be a ""stressed bench.""","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, Option A is the only one that respects the structural limits of the bay and the instability of our power systems. It is the logical choice.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"I think we are all starting to agree. Option A is gentle on the staff, the building, and the budget. It's a lovely choice.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,Yay! I'm so glad we're on the same page! Option A is just so cheerful and community-focused. I love it!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Victoria,,It is the only option that doesn't ignore the reality of our staffing crisis. I feel much more comfortable with this.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shion,,"It's not the most daring choice, but the presence of the craftspeople satisfies my requirement for human interaction. It's acceptable.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Asuka,,It is more than acceptable; it is the only responsible choice. It ensures the building remains functional and safe.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shizue,,It warms my heart to see us reach a consensus so kindly. Option A will be a wonderful experience for our visitors.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'm voting for A! Let's make it happen!,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I am voting for A. It is the only rational path forward.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shion,,I'll go with A. It's better than a boring static show or a dangerous one.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Asuka,,My vote is for A. It is the only proposal that fits the physical constraints of the gallery.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I also vote for A. It's a safe, lovely, and reliable plan.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
